# R287 — completion marker contract and failed-wrapper accounting

Actual gpt-6-astra; planning only. ROOT must review before any implementation.

The frozen producer writes `observations.assertions_completed`. The R285 runner instead indexes a nonexistent top-level `assertions_completed` during final assessment. The actual sidecar has top-level presence=false/value=null and nested presence=true/value=true. These are separate observations.

The sole memory invocation remains a wrapper failure (exit 1), with no normal result.json. Its existing JUnit records one PASS and its stdout reports 181.29 seconds. Reaching the consumer through the frozen short-circuit expression implies an in-memory child exit of 0, but this is source inference, not a separately persisted process receipt. No final result, process cleanup status or full T2 acceptance may be invented.

## Narrow source preparation

The same sole Sol may create a **new-path** corrected runner after ROOT accepts applicability. Preserve the R285 runner and every original candidate/native/report. Read the nested boolean only, with exact type/presence checks, and keep the top-level missing fact separately. Missing or malformed nested data fails eligibility; it must not become an observed False, a fallback, or a raw-data edit.

Retain all other original acceptance checks. Protect only the derived assessment/result-persistence boundary so an ordinary assessment exception records its true failure and attempts fail-closed result persistence. Preserve reservation, child launch, cleanup, AUTHOR spend and the resource-consumer semantics. No generic pipeline or product/fixture/plugin change.

Save complete before bytes/base64/mode, a persistent candidate before native Add, actual native arguments/return, after pin, limited diff and a concise change report. Prove all bytes outside the completion helper and final-assessment boundary unchanged. The corrected runner is **not executed in this round**.

## Existing-evidence assessment and accounting

ROOT may prepare one independent, fully reviewed stdlib metadata script, then run it once with the plan's exact absolute interpreter/cwd and 120-second bound; stdout is capped at 6000 UTF-8 bytes. This is not a test slot.

It must independently check the existing raw receipt/XML/cases/resources/source generations and four new DB/archive pairs with twelve absent sidecars, without SQL or modifying old bytes. Resource summary counts (542 attempts, 540 initialized, 542 cleanup) remain reported until their actual lifecycle evidence is checked. Missing process fields remain unavailable.

Write only new R287 assessment/settlement evidence. Do not backfill the old result or replay the wrapper. Fullbefore/CAS changes only the original ROOT memory key from RESERVED 1/0 to SPENT_UNEXPECTED_WRAPPER_FINALIZATION_FAILURE 1/0. AUTHOR stays SPENT; the other two keys stay HELD. Any failed metadata attempt is preserved and stops without retry.

## Boundaries and generations

All 29 fixed inputs, the 260 identity/scope proofs and complete physical archives are pinned in input-observation.json and before/manifest.json. The initial draft observation is retained separately; its default-based cleanup entries are excluded from final proof claims. Planner has not independently validated every resource lifecycle.

Product27/protected211, test193f, plugin, old raw, historical missing35/null and database evidence remain untouched. Only exact known old-pin/full-archive mappings may resolve a legitimate ROOT/context transition; no path exemption.

After the sequence stops, ROOT may fullbefore/CAS-update only factual planning.R285/R287 and append PHASE, linking actual failures/source acceptance and retaining unrelated fields. T2/T12/native/formal remain unaccepted.

No new runtime, static, review or Git budget is granted. A later actual Astra continuation must explicitly bind any new execution to its source generation and finite budget; the failed memory slot is never reusable. Freeze this plan and STOP for ROOT review.

